laurel 9016 (iOS 26): a late CPU: what it last did, and where it comes in

[V logs/usblog-20261103-071332.txt] 12 of 12 stackshots given up, in 4 boots, name CPU 5, and the line says nothing more. ml_dbgwrap_* is UNSUPPORTED on this SoC and EDPCSR is not safe to read (laurel_wdog.c, docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md).
After LAUREL DEBUG ACK: on: stackshot given up: two lines per late CPU (last interrupt, its thread, SGI pending or not). When that CPU takes the signal: LAUREL DEBUG ACK: on: cpu N came M ms after ...: pc lr fp: the first point where it let interrupts in.

